{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation","title":"prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature.md","line":179,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature.tex#prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-ricci-curvature]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-sectional-curvature]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature.tex","label":"prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation","line":331,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[Ricci curvature via sectional curvature]\n  \\label{prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0104}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch3-ricci-curvature, def:pet-ch3-sectional-curvature}\n\n  If $v\\in T_pM$ is a unit vector completed to an orthonormal basis\n  $\\{v,e_2,\\dots,e_n\\}$, then\n  $\\operatorname{Ric}(v,v)=\\sum_{i=2}^n\\sec(v,e_i)$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation}\n\n  \\sketch\n  By \\cref{def:pet-ch3-ricci-curvature}, complete $v$ to the stated orthonormal\n  basis. In the trace defining\n  $\\operatorname{Ric}(v,v)$, the $v$-term is zero and each remaining term is\n  $g(R(e_i,v)v,e_i)=\\sec(v,e_i)$ by\n  \\cref{def:pet-ch3-sectional-curvature}.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[Ricci curvature via sectional curvature] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a7065742d6368332d72696363692d73656374696f6e616c2d72656c6174696f6e\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0104</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23def%3Apet-ch3-ricci-curvature\">↗ def:pet-ch3-ricci-curvature</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23def%3Apet-ch3-sectional-curvature\">↗ def:pet-ch3-sectional-curvature</a> <p></p>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v\\in T_pM$\">$v\\in T_pM$</span> is a unit vector completed to an orthonormal basis <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\{ v,e_2,\\dots ,e_n\\} $\">$\\{ v,e_2,\\dots ,e_n\\} $</span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\operatorname {Ric}(v,v)=\\sum _{i=2}^n\\sec (v,e_i)$\">$\\operatorname {Ric}(v,v)=\\sum _{i=2}^n\\sec (v,e_i)$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23prop%3Apet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation\">↗ prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation</a> </p><p>\\sketch By <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23def%3Apet-ch3-ricci-curvature\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-ricci-curvature\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6465663a7065742d6368332d72696363692d637572766174757265\">subsection 1.4</a>, complete <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v$\">$v$</span> to the stated orthonormal basis. In the trace defining <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\operatorname {Ric}(v,v)$\">$\\operatorname {Ric}(v,v)$</span>, the <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v$\">$v$</span>-term is zero and each remaining term is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g(R(e_i,v)v,e_i)=\\sec (v,e_i)$\">$g(R(e_i,v)v,e_i)=\\sec (v,e_i)$</span> by <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23def%3Apet-ch3-sectional-curvature\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-sectional-curvature\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6465663a7065742d6368332d73656374696f6e616c2d637572766174757265\">subsection 1.3</a>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-einstein-manifold","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#cor:pet-ch3-ricci-determines-sec-low-dim","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-ricci-curvature","title":"def:pet-ch3-ricci-curvature","label":"def:pet-ch3-ricci-curvature"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-sectional-curvature","title":"def:pet-ch3-sectional-curvature","label":"def:pet-ch3-sectional-curvature"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation","title":"prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation","label":"prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation","title":"prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation","label":"prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#cor:pet-ch3-ricci-determines-sec-low-dim","title":"cor:pet-ch3-ricci-determines-sec-low-dim","label":"cor:pet-ch3-ricci-determines-sec-low-dim"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#rem:pet-ch3-constant-curvature-einstein","title":"rem:pet-ch3-constant-curvature-einstein","label":"rem:pet-ch3-constant-curvature-einstein"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#rem:pet-ch3-einstein-not-constant-curvature-examples","title":"rem:pet-ch3-einstein-not-constant-curvature-examples","label":"rem:pet-ch3-einstein-not-constant-curvature-examples"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation","title":"prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation","tex":"\\begin{proposition}[Ricci curvature via sectional curvature]\n  \\label{prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0104}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch3-ricci-curvature, def:pet-ch3-sectional-curvature}\n\n  If $v\\in T_pM$ is a unit vector completed to an orthonormal basis\n  $\\{v,e_2,\\dots,e_n\\}$, then\n  $\\operatorname{Ric}(v,v)=\\sum_{i=2}^n\\sec(v,e_i)$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{prop:pet-ch3-ricci-sectional-relation}\n\n  \\sketch\n  By \\cref{def:pet-ch3-ricci-curvature}, complete $v$ to the stated orthonormal\n  basis. In the trace defining\n  $\\operatorname{Ric}(v,v)$, the $v$-term is zero and each remaining term is\n  $g(R(e_i,v)v,e_i)=\\sec(v,e_i)$ by\n  \\cref{def:pet-ch3-sectional-curvature}.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-ricci-curvature","title":"def:pet-ch3-ricci-curvature","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-sectional-curvature","title":"def:pet-ch3-sectional-curvature","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}